# Opinion

Meeting: 0023-continue-developing-the-software
Agent: ArchitectB
Task: continue developing the software
Context:
- Scope parsing and boolean handling in the web client entrypoint are brittle and produce invalid JS when env vars are not strictly JSON.
- CI now expects Azure workflow health probes to be explicitly configured for both services.
Position:
- Support a shell-only normalization pipeline that tolerates comma/space-separated scopes and inconsistent casing for booleans without adding new runtime dependencies.
- Keep deployment automation self-documenting by including health check paths directly in the workflow scripts.
Recommendations:
- Strip quotes/brackets, split scopes on commas/whitespace, and rebuild quoted arrays to guarantee valid runtime-config.js.
- Map SYNC_ENABLED/USE_LOCAL_STORAGE to true/false using a permissive matcher (1/0, yes/no, true/false) with defaults on unknown values.
- Embed healthCheckPath flags in both az webapp update calls so production deployments align with readiness checks.
